<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan's CPC sells Nov fuel oil at near $120/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's CPC sells Nov fuel oil at near $120/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has awarded a sell tender for 30,000 tonnes of November fuel oil at close to $120 per tonne free-on-board (FOB) Kaohsiung, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>CPC sold the cargo of 3.0-percent sulphur, 180-centistoke fuel oil for lifting November 14-18.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold a 30,000-tonne cargo of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil for loading October 1-10 at $116 per tonne FOB Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082).</p>
